{"wireMagic": "pb3", "events": [{"tStartMs": 2380, "dDurationMs": 7360, "segs": [{"utf8": "Hello, and welcome to the Junkyard Love Podcast.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 9740, "dDurationMs": 32520, "segs": [{"utf8": "Oh, what is Gucci, my dude skis?\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 42260, "dDurationMs": 1560, "segs": [{"utf8": "This is the Junkyard Love Podcast.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 43820, "dDurationMs": 6160, "segs": [{"utf8": "Today I'm going to start this off with just a small excerpt from Yvonne Harari's Sapiens,\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 49980, "dDurationMs": 2000, "segs": [{"utf8": "a brief history of humankind.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 51980, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "It's a great book.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 52980, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "I haven't made my way all the way through it yet, but we discussed some us and they\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 56980, "dDurationMs": 6200, "segs": [{"utf8": "and them in the coming episodes of the podcast, so this excerpt here just kind\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 63180, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "of stood out to me.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 64180, "dDurationMs": 2400, "segs": [{"utf8": "I'm going to read this right after the end of this.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 66580, "dDurationMs": 3080, "segs": [{"utf8": "We'll get right going into the episode with my buddy Trenton Kessler, excited for you\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 69660, "dDurationMs": 2510, "segs": [{"utf8": "guys to hear this one.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 72170, "dDurationMs": 3000, "segs": [{"utf8": "The global vision.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 75170, "dDurationMs": 4600, "segs": [{"utf8": "From a practical perspective, the most important stage in the process of global unification\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 79770, "dDurationMs": 4600, "segs": [{"utf8": "occurred in the last few centuries, when empires grew and trades intensified.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 84370, "dDurationMs": 4440, "segs": [{"utf8": "Ever-tightening links were formed between the people of Afro-Asia, America, Australia,\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 88810, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "and Oceania.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 89810, "dDurationMs": 4520, "segs": [{"utf8": "Thus, Mexican chili peppers made it into the Indian food, and Spanish cattle began grazing\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 94330, "dDurationMs": 1680, "segs": [{"utf8": "in Argentina.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 96010, "dDurationMs": 3840, "segs": [{"utf8": "Yet from an ideological perspective, an even more important development occurred during\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 99850, "dDurationMs": 4560, "segs": [{"utf8": "the first millennium BC, when the idea of a universal order took root.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 104410, "dDurationMs": 4340, "segs": [{"utf8": "For thousands of years previously, history was already moving slowly in the directions\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 108750, "dDurationMs": 4900, "segs": [{"utf8": "of global unity, but the idea of a universal order governing the entire world was still\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 113650, "dDurationMs": 3440, "segs": [{"utf8": "alien to most people.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 117090, "dDurationMs": 5840, "segs": [{"utf8": "Homo sapiens evolved to think of people as divided into us and them.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 122930, "dDurationMs": 5640, "segs": [{"utf8": "This was the group immediately around you, whoever you were, and them was everyone else.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 128570, "dDurationMs": 4080, "segs": [{"utf8": "In fact, no social animal is ever guided by the interests of the entire species to which\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 132650, "dDurationMs": 1240, "segs": [{"utf8": "it belongs.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 133890, "dDurationMs": 4060, "segs": [{"utf8": "No chimpanzee cares about the interests of the chimpanzee species.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 137950, "dDurationMs": 3340, "segs": [{"utf8": "No snail will lift a tentacle for the global snail community.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 141290, "dDurationMs": 5200, "segs": [{"utf8": "No lion alpha male makes a bid for becoming the king of all lions, and at the entrance\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 146490, "dDurationMs": 5570, "segs": [{"utf8": "of no beehive can one find the slogan, Worker Bees of the World, Unite.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 152060, "dDurationMs": 4080, "segs": [{"utf8": "But beginning with the cognitive revolution, Homo sapiens became more and more exceptional\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 156140, "dDurationMs": 1680, "segs": [{"utf8": "in this respect.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 157820, "dDurationMs": 4520, "segs": [{"utf8": "People began to cooperate on a regular basis with complete strangers, whom they imagined\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 162340, "dDurationMs": 2120, "segs": [{"utf8": "as brothers or friends.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 164460, "dDurationMs": 2320, "segs": [{"utf8": "Yet this brotherhood was not universal.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 166780, "dDurationMs": 4440, "segs": [{"utf8": "Somewhere in the next valley or beyond the mountain range, one could still sense them.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 171220, "dDurationMs": 4840, "segs": [{"utf8": "When the first pharaoh, Minis, united Egypt around 3000 BC, it was clear to the\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 176060, "dDurationMs": 4840, "segs": [{"utf8": "Egyptians that Egypt had a border, and beyond the border lurked barbarians.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 180900, "dDurationMs": 4080, "segs": [{"utf8": "The barbarians were alien, threatening, and interesting only to the extent that they had\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 184980, "dDurationMs": 3600, "segs": [{"utf8": "land or natural resources that the Egyptians wanted.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 188580, "dDurationMs": 6220, "segs": [{"utf8": "All the imagined orders people created tended to ignore a substantial part of humankind.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 194800, "dDurationMs": 4520, "segs": [{"utf8": "The first millennium BC witnessed the appearance of three potentially universal orders, whose\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 199320, "dDurationMs": 4960, "segs": [{"utf8": "devotees could for the first time imagine the entire world and the entire human race\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 204280, "dDurationMs": 4400, "segs": [{"utf8": "as a single unit governed by a single set of laws.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 208680, "dDurationMs": 2800, "segs": [{"utf8": "One was us, at least potentially.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 211480, "dDurationMs": 1680, "segs": [{"utf8": "There was no longer them.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 213160, "dDurationMs": 4240, "segs": [{"utf8": "The first universal order to appear was economic, the monetary order.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 217400, "dDurationMs": 3440, "segs": [{"utf8": "The second universal order was political, the imperial order.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 220840, "dDurationMs": 3960, "segs": [{"utf8": "The third universal order was religious, the order of universal religions such as\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 224800, "dDurationMs": 2560, "segs": [{"utf8": "Buddhism, Christianity, and Islam.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 227360, "dDurationMs": 3600, "segs": [{"utf8": "Merchants, conquerors, and prophets were the first people who managed to transcend\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 230960, "dDurationMs": 4920, "segs": [{"utf8": "the binary evolutionary division, us versus them, and to foresee the potential unity\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 235880, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "of humankind.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 237440, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "For the merchants, the entire world was a single market and all humans were potential\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 241440, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "customers.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 242440, "dDurationMs": 3840, "segs": [{"utf8": "They tried to establish an economic order that would apply to all, everywhere.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 246280, "dDurationMs": 4120, "segs": [{"utf8": "For the conquerors, the entire world was a single empire and all humans were potential\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 250400, "dDurationMs": 1000, "segs": [{"utf8": "subjects.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 251400, "dDurationMs": 3320, "segs": [{"utf8": "And for the prophets, the entire world held a single truth and all humans were\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 254720, "dDurationMs": 1680, "segs": [{"utf8": "potential believers.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 256400, "dDurationMs": 5760, "segs": [{"utf8": "They too tried to establish an order that would be applicable for everyone and everywhere.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 262160, "dDurationMs": 3720, "segs": [{"utf8": "During the last three millennia, people made more and more ambitious attempts to\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 265880, "dDurationMs": 2080, "segs": [{"utf8": "realize that global vision.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 267960, "dDurationMs": 3440, "segs": [{"utf8": "The next three chapters discuss how money, empires, and universal religion spread,\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 271400, "dDurationMs": 2640, "segs": [{"utf8": "this referring to the book itself, and how they laid the foundation of the\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 274040, "dDurationMs": 1680, "segs": [{"utf8": "United World of today.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 275720, "dDurationMs": 3160, "segs": [{"utf8": "We begin with the story of the greatest conqueror in history, a conqueror\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 278880, "dDurationMs": 3800, "segs": [{"utf8": "possessed of extreme tolerance and adaptability, which consequently managed\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 282680, "dDurationMs": 2480, "segs": [{"utf8": "to gain the allegiance of all people.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 285160, "dDurationMs": 2320, "segs": [{"utf8": "This conqueror is money.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 287480, "dDurationMs": 3760, "segs": [{"utf8": "People who do not believe in the same God or obey the same king are more than\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 291240, "dDurationMs": 1920, "segs": [{"utf8": "willing to use the same money.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 293200, "dDurationMs": 5700, "segs": [{"utf8": "Osama bin Laden, for all of his hatred of American culture, American religion,\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 298900, "dDurationMs": 3960, "segs": [{"utf8": "and American politics, was very fond of American dollars.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 302860, "dDurationMs": 4490, "segs": [{"utf8": "How did money succeed where gods and kings failed?\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 307350, "dDurationMs": 3240, "segs": [{"utf8": "Enjoy the episode.\n"}]}, {"tStartMs": 310590, "dDurationMs": 1920, "segs": 